# Netlify serves the repo root, so every file here is public by default.
# Block what should not be, before any bytes leave the edge.
#
# Netlify already skips dotfiles and dot-directories -- .publish_state.json,
# .github/, .claude/ and .gitnexus/ all 404 without a rule. Everything else
# needs one. Every rule is forced (404!) because Netlify serves a matching
# static file in preference to a redirect; without the "!" these rules are
# silently dead for exactly the files that need blocking.
#
# Rules are explicit paths rather than extension globs, because
# Netlify only supports a trailing splat, not patterns like /*.py.

# --- Subscriber list -------------------------------------------------------
# Lives in the repo because the announcer routine reads it from git; it has
# no business being downloadable from the web.
/subscribers.txt                /404.html   404!

# --- Publishing pipeline source -------------------------------------------
# No secrets (the service-account key is gitignored), but these expose Drive
# folder IDs, the GA property, and the shape of the automation.
/publish.py                     /404.html   404!
/publish_review.py              /404.html   404!
/auth.py                        /404.html   404!
/scripts/*                      /404.html   404!
/n8n/*                          /404.html   404!

# --- Operational notes -----------------------------------------------------
/CLAUDE.md                      /404.html   404!
/AGENTS.md                      /404.html   404!
/README.md                      /404.html   404!
/PublishInstructions.md         /404.html   404!
/PublishReviewInstructions.md   /404.html   404!
/AUTOMATION-NOTES.md            /404.html   404!
/social-media-posts.md          /404.html   404!
/rebrand.patch                  /404.html   404!

# --- Retired -------------------------------------------------------------
# MyPubs-PDFs/ was 300 MB of unlinked PDFs and is no longer in the repo.
# Kept as a guard so re-adding it does not silently put it back on the web:
# bandwidth is metered at 20 credits/GB against a 300-credit month, so one
# full crawl of that directory cost ~6 credits.
/MyPubs-PDFs/*                  /404.html   404!
